---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AssetAllocationLab from "../../components/AssetAllocationLab.tsx";
import NextTool from "../../components/NextTool.astro";
import Sources from "../../components/Sources.astro";
import "../../styles/simtool.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much in Stocks?"
  description="The single biggest investing decision is your stock/bond mix. Slide the dial and see the historical trade-off — more stocks means higher long-run growth but deeper, scarier drops — plus the volatility drag that rewards a smoother ride."
>
  <section class="container wl-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interactive Tool</p>
    <h1>How much should be in stocks?</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Which funds you pick matters far less than one dial: how much of your money
      rides in stocks versus bonds. Turn it and watch the trade-off that governs
      every portfolio — more stocks lifts your long-run return, but you have to
      survive a deeper drop to collect it. The right answer isn't the highest
      return; it's the most risk you can actually hold onto through the worst of it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-host">
    <AssetAllocationLab client:load />
  </section>

  <section class="container wl-explainer">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Three questions set your mix</h2>
      <p>
        There's no universally "right" allocation — there's the right one for you,
        and it comes down to three dimensions of risk:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Ability</strong> — how long is your horizon? A 30-year-old has
          decades to recover from a crash; someone spending the money next year does
          not. Longer horizons can hold more stocks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Willingness</strong> — can you actually sit through the worst
          drop on the chart without selling? A perfect plan you abandon at the
          bottom is worse than a modest plan you keep. Be honest.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Need</strong> — do your goals even require the extra risk? If a
          60/40 mix comfortably funds your life, reaching for 100% stocks may be
          taking risk you're not being paid to take.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why a smoother ride compounds to more</h2>
      <p>
        The tool shows a quiet but crucial gap: a portfolio's <em>average</em>
        yearly return is always higher than what it actually <strong>compounds</strong>
        to. That difference — <strong>volatility drag</strong> — grows with roughly
        half the variance, because losses hurt more than equal gains help: a −50%
        year needs a +100% year just to break even. Cutting needless volatility
        lifts the return you keep at the same average. It's the mathematical heart
        of "diversify, and don't bear risk you aren't paid for." Educational only,
        not financial advice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Sources tool="asset-allocation" />

  <NextTool current="/tools/asset-allocation" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .wl-intro {
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-md);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .wl-explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }
</style>

<style is:global>
  .ss-headline {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding: var(--space-sm) var(--space-md);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .ss-headline-label {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-headline-value {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .ss-headline-sub {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }
  .ss-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
  }
  .ss-stats > div {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .ss-stats dt {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }
  .ss-stats dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
